  "title": "Unified Title",
  "summary": "COBRA-Skills and When Synthetic Data Hurts are both focused on optimizing agent skill performance through efficient frameworks and addressing challenges in skill retrieval for LLM agents.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "COBRA-Skills introduces a framework for skill optimization using contextual-bandit-guided prioritization and evidence-based evolution, achieving strong performance with reduced cost compared to existing methods.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "When synthetic data hinders skill retrieval, the study shows that synthetic data fine-tuning improves in-distribution retrieval but causes catastrophic forgetting on real and out-of-distribution data.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The study evaluates several forgetting mitigation techniques, including embedding-anchor regularization, LwF, EWC, and L2-initialization, and demonstrates their effectiveness in both in-distribution and synthetic data scenarios.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
